message: "If you use this survey or its companion artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Resolving Evidence Chains in Multi-Hop RAG: A Challenge-Centered Survey"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Luo
    given-names: Yuqing
    affiliation: University of Science and Technology of China
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Kai
    affiliation: University of Science and Technology of China
  - family-names: Yang
    given-names: Heli
    affiliation: University of Science and Technology of China
year: 2026
abstract: >-
  A challenge-centered survey of multi-hop retrieval-augmented generation
  defined by dependency among external evidence units. The survey separates
  Next-Hop Discovery, Path Management, Evidence Sufficiency, Error Recovery,
  and Evidence Composition, and analyzes a canonical evidence map of 208
  reviewed works with 135 Core works used for quantitative challenge analysis.
keywords:
  - multi-hop RAG
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - multi-hop question answering
  - evidence dependency
  - evidence chains
  - agentic retrieval
license: MIT
notes: >-
  Author manuscript draft targeting ACM Transactions on Information Systems.
  Review cutoff: 2026-08-09. Add repository DOI and final publisher metadata
